  "notes": {
    "manas-2010:p1630:b001:l007": "San is an epic multitude unit, retained without an invented exact conversion; likewise later san and ilek quantities.",
    "manas-2010:p1630:b001:l013": "Printed Күн Жаң-Жуң retained as Kün Jangjung, not silently harmonized with Ay Jangjung elsewhere. Döödür retained as a separate named giant.",
    "manas-2010:p1630:b001:l020": "Kalcha functions as Kongurbay’s recurring epithet here, not a newly introduced person; attachment can vary elsewhere.",
    "manas-2010:p1630:b001:l026": "Printed ат оюнча read contextually as the skilled horseman formula ат оюнчу; source spelling retained in extraction.",
    "manas-2010:p1630:b001:l034": "Kanzharkol retained as the named fighter; shortened Kanzhar at1631:42 is not a separate person.",
    "manas-2010:p1631:b001:l021": "Printed Ayba retained; later1644 has Eybe. Identity is not proven by spelling alone.",
    "manas-2010:p1631:b001:l026": "Орокто- denotes bobbing/dipping motion, including riding: Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/орок/.",
    "manas-2010:p1631:b001:l027": "Корокто- denotes sticking/protruding upward: Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/корок/. Commanders are the grammatical subject here;1641:20 explicitly supplies their lances.",
    "manas-2010:p1631:b001:l035": "Кечил rendered shaven ones, a religious/cultural designation, not identification of every combatant as an ordained monk.",
    "manas-2010:p1632:b001:l015": "Printed сен балбан is read contextually as сан балбан, a san of champions, in the surrounding host-enumeration formula. This contextual correction is uncertain; printed сен (you) remains in the raw source. Калдай is governor, not a personal name.",
    "manas-2010:p1632:b001:l023": "Кызыталак retained as an abusive epithet (bastard), including when applied sympathetically to a Muslim hero; not omitted.",
    "manas-2010:p1632:b001:l028": "Кек бүтөп is syntactically rough; revenge over the governor’s killing is the contextual reading, not a confidently restored text.",
    "manas-2010:p1633:b001:l002": "Чалмачаны read as the lasso-bearing attack, with the final ы morphologically irregular. Yudakhin чалмачан means bearing a lasso: https://el-sozduk.kg/чалмачан/. No turban or garment inferred.",
    "manas-2010:p1633:b001:l007": "Forty-two khans retained literally, not harmonized with forty tribes.",
    "manas-2010:p1633:b001:l018": "Almambet’s absence is retained despite his later arrival; other heroes’ repeated absence/presence statements are likewise not suppressed.",
    "manas-2010:p1633:b001:l028": "Кынай intensifies the sword’s excellence contextually; exact adverbial form uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1633:b001:l029": "Six sword names and their stated bearers are retained as printed. Zulpukor is assigned to Manas here, but1643:12 gives a double-edged zulpukor to Kongurbay; generic epithet versus individual weapon is uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1633:b001:l032": "Printed Жойкума retained as Zhoykuma;1642:28 has Ойкума, Oykuma. No silent normalization.",
    "manas-2010:p1634:b001:l015": "Mirror of the shoulder-blade is the source’s weapon image, not a literal added mirror.",
    "manas-2010:p1634:b001:l018": "Очогор is a matchlock:2015 explanatory dictionary explicitly mentions a wick https://el-sozduk.kg/очогор/.",
    "manas-2010:p1634:b001:l020": "Сур келте rendered descriptively short gray gun; whether a unique weapon-name here is uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1634:b001:l037": "Аруудай rendered pure/fair, retaining comparison with purity rather than supplying an unattested animal.",
    "manas-2010:p1634:b001:l042": "Тулга means a three-legged cooking-pot support: Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/tulga/. Its imagined placement on the neck is retained as an unsettling captivity image; not silently altered to туулга, helmet. Exact device/use uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1635:b001:l003": "Кембайла- means lead under guard; кембай is escort/convoy: Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/кембай/. Кудайга is retained as to God, though attachment beside the preceding Chinese dative is awkward and its intended religious referent remains uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1635:b001:l004": "Source says height forty kez followed by very deep and a pit; height/depth inconsistency retained. Kez rendered cubits without metric conversion.",
    "manas-2010:p1635:b001:l007": "Капкайда rendered far away; no unsupported ancient/grievance chronology supplied.",
    "manas-2010:p1635:b001:l018": "Эше чаап read as sweeping aside with the coat-skirt from the immediately preceding line; exact action uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1635:b001:l025": "Möndü retained as the explicit battle cry, not treated as a wholly untranslated utterance.",
    "manas-2010:p1635:b001:l030": "Cow-like tail-root is the printed horse-anatomy epithet, not an assertion that Sarala has a cow’s tail.",
    "manas-2010:p1636:b001:l021": "Mangküsh is a separate named fighter here:1642 explicitly mounts him on a rhinoceros and narrates his beheading before Kongurbay reacts. Although Yudakhin маңкүш can mean a simpleton https://el-sozduk.kg/маңк/, that common-noun sense does not replace the demonstrated name.",
    "manas-2010:p1636:b001:l037": "Printed эреннң has irregular final letters; read as the possessive hero formula contextually, without altering extraction.",
    "manas-2010:p1637:b001:l008": "Chubak placed on Almambet’s right knee is retained literally; not changed to conventional pillion seating.",
    "manas-2010:p1637:b001:l031": "Azireti Aaly retained as the Islamic heroic figure named by the poem; no historical proof of his journey asserted.",
    "manas-2010:p1638:b001:l006": "Printed Каргылуу read provisionally through the parallel Карылуу at1638:1 as a strength epithet. The extra г and possible literal collar sense remain unresolved; raw spelling unchanged.",
    "manas-2010:p1638:b001:l017": "Казыналык understood as treasury/state service in this marksman’s appointment; exact institution unverified.",
    "manas-2010:p1638:b001:l020": "Six thousand dying followed by six surviving is the printed arithmetic; no repair to5,994.",
    "manas-2010:p1638:b001:l028": "Bulletproof inner flesh and putting on protection are retained across these lines; the exact magic/garment mechanism is not supplied.",
    "manas-2010:p1638:b001:l036": "Кезик rendered fever without imposing a modern diagnosis. The unexpressed hearer is probably Almambet, but the narrative subject remains grammatically uncertain.",
    "manas-2010:p1639:b001:l003": "Тартпаган has an unexpressed object; withdrawing is provisional, while drawing/pulling a weapon is also possible.",
    "manas-2010:p1639:b001:l007": "Karykan retained as the named possessor of the weather-stone; no identification with a historical person.",
    "manas-2010:p1639:b001:l015": "The comparison to whimpering girls retains the source’s disparaging gender image.",
    "manas-2010:p1639:b001:l031": "Printed Akayar retained, not silently changed to Agayar elsewhere.",
    "manas-2010:p1639:b001:l035": "Alabash is named among steeds without a stated rider here; no owner invented.",
    "manas-2010:p1640:b001:l008": "Munaryk provisionally treated as the desert’s name here; elsewhere мунарык describes haze. Capitalization alone is not proof of a separate geography.",
    "manas-2010:p1641:b001:l002": "Таш сайынган denotes the rank bead of Chinese/Kalmyk officials: Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/tash-8/. No idol-worship inference.",
    "manas-2010:p1641:b001:l003": "Тазаларын means their best in this formula, not bald men: Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/ТАЗ/.",
    "manas-2010:p1641:b001:l030": "It-Ölbös retained as the named battle desert; forty days is journey duration, not a measured distance.",
    "manas-2010:p1641:b001:l037": "Swan ears burning is retained as the source’s hyperbolic desert image.",
    "manas-2010:p1642:b001:l008": "Керик rendered rhinoceros; the extraordinary mount is not replaced with a horse.",
    "manas-2010:p1642:b001:l023": "Буй кылган rendered threw into turmoil; related Yudakhin буйкыл https://el-sozduk.kg/buy-9/.",
    "manas-2010:p1642:b001:l028": "Printed Oykuma retained beside Zhoykuma at1633:32; weapon-spelling variation documented.",
    "manas-2010:p1642:b001:l038": "Айдар is a retained tuft of hair; nape location is explicit here, even though forelock is the recurring English epithet.",
    "manas-2010:p1643:b001:l012": "Printed lowercase зулпукор with Kongurbay retained; this may be a sword type/epithet rather than the unique Manas weapon listed1633:29.",
    "manas-2010:p1643:b001:l019": "Teeth crumbling like millet retained literally; not silently softened to chattering.",
